    "content": "Dawn Staley is the head coach of the South Carolina Gamecocks women's basketball team, a position she has held since May 2008. A Basketball Hall of Famer, she has built a dynasty, winning three NCAA National Championships (2017, 2022, 2024) and leading the team to multiple Final Four appearances, including 2026. Key facts about Coach Dawn Staley: Career Success: She is a three-time Naismith National Coach of the Year and has led South Carolina to numerous SEC regular season and tournament championships. Highest Paid: As of Jan. 17, 2025, Staley signed a contract extension making her the highest-paid coach in women’s college basketball. Playing Career: A legendary point guard, she was a two-time Naismith Player of the Year at Virginia and a three-time Olympic gold medalist. USA Basketball: She served as the head coach for the U.S. Women's National Team, winning a gold medal at the 2020 Tokyo Olympics. Legacy: Known for transforming the South Carolina program into a national powerhouse and advocating for, diversity, equity, and equality in women's basketball. Under her leadership, the Gamecocks have become a consistent national title contender.",
